WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:07.800 align:start position:19%
Number one, the undisputed champion of
weird food.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:12.840 align:start position:19%
Casu marzu.
From the island of Sardinia, Italy. The

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:18.640 align:start position:19%
name literally means
rotten cheese.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:24.600 align:start position:19%
It starts as normal sheep's milk cheese.
Then they introduce cheese fly larvae.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:29.880 align:start position:19%
Thousands of them.
The maggots digest the cheese from the

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.120 align:start position:19%
inside, breaking down the fats until it
turns soft and gooey.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:39.480 align:start position:19%
When served, the maggots are still
alive,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.840 align:start position:19%
wriggling in your food
right now.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:48.000 align:start position:19%
Some say the maggots must be alive when
you eat it. Dead maggots mean the cheese

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:52.040 align:start position:19%
has gone bad.
Disturb them and they launch up to 6 in

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.680 align:start position:19%
into the air.
That's why you shield your eyes.

